# NEAR security (agents)

- Never request, log, or commit seed phrases, private keys, or `.env` secrets.
- Default to sandbox/local (`pnpm demo`) or read-only RPC; mainnet only with explicit human approval.
- Do not use `near-mcp` `system_import_account` or transaction-signing tools without user approval.
- Do not assume `Final` until receipt/status verified; handle cross-contract callback failures.
- Validate attached deposits, gas, and authorization on every contract change method.
- Separate view calls from state-changing calls in docs and generated code.
- Run `.agents/skills/near-contract-audit/` before mainnet contract changes.
- Never fabricate deployment addresses, tx hashes, or passing tests.
